Automatic closing of brackets and quotes (decision NB5.1). Scripts start with `AutoClose`: the window turns it on
by its setting, the other scripts type without it.

=== an opener inserts its closer with the caret between
--- before
#% cell
▮
--- keys
AutoClose "f("
--- after
#% cell
f(▮)

=== every bracket kind pairs
--- before
#% cell
▮
--- keys
AutoClose "[{("
--- after
#% cell
[{(▮)}]

=== typing the closer steps over the automatic one
--- before
#% cell
▮
--- keys
AutoClose "f(x)"
--- after
#% cell
f(x)▮

=== nested pairs are stepped over in turn
--- before
#% cell
▮
--- keys
AutoClose "g([1, 2])+1"
--- after
#% cell
g([1, 2])+1▮

=== a closer that was not inserted automatically is typed
--- before
#% cell
a▮)
--- keys
AutoClose ")"
--- after
#% cell
a)▮)

=== Backspace after an opener deletes its untouched closer too
--- before
#% cell
x▮
--- keys
AutoClose "(" Backspace
--- after
#% cell
x▮

=== after typing over the closer Backspace deletes one character
--- before
#% cell
x▮
--- keys
AutoClose "(a)" Backspace
--- after
#% cell
x(a▮

=== an opener before a name does not pair
--- before
#% cell
▮x
--- keys
AutoClose "("
--- after
#% cell
(▮x

=== an opener with a selection wraps it and keeps it selected
--- before
#% cell
⟦a+b⟧*c
--- keys
AutoClose "("
--- after
#% cell
(⟦a+b⟧)*c

=== a quote pairs before the end, a space or a closer
--- before
#% cell
f(▮)
--- keys
AutoClose "\"" "ab" "\""
--- after
#% cell
f("ab"▮)

=== a quote before a name does not pair
--- before
#% cell
▮x
--- keys
AutoClose "\""
--- after
#% cell
"▮x

=== a quote with a selection wraps it
--- before
#% cell
⟦hi⟧
--- keys
AutoClose "\""
--- after
#% cell
"⟦hi⟧"

=== no brackets are paired inside a string
--- before
#% cell
"a ▮"
--- keys
AutoClose "("
--- after
#% cell
"a (▮"

=== no brackets are paired inside a comment
--- before
#% cell
x # see ▮
--- keys
AutoClose "["
--- after
#% cell
x # see [▮

=== a prime is not paired
--- before
#% cell
▮
--- keys
AutoClose "f'"
--- after
#% cell
f'▮

=== undo removes the pair in one step
--- before
#% cell
x▮
--- keys
AutoClose "(" Ctrl+Z
--- after
#% cell
x▮

=== moving the caret forgets the automatic closers
--- before
#% cell
▮
--- keys
AutoClose "(" Left Right ")"
--- after
#% cell
()▮)

=== an opener at the insertion point makes a cell with the pair
--- before
‖
--- keys
AutoClose "("
--- after
#% cell
(▮)

=== prose cells pair brackets but keep their smart quotes
--- before
#% text
# ▮
--- keys
AutoClose "(\"a"
--- after
#% text
# (“a▮)

=== without the setting nothing is paired
--- before
#% cell
▮
--- keys
"f("
--- after
#% cell
f(▮

=== a closer typed after a box inside automatic brackets steps over the automatic one (round 34)
--- before
#% cell
x
‖
--- keys
AutoClose "(" Ctrl+2 "5" Ctrl+Space " + 1)" Ctrl+/ "2"
--- boxes
((√(5) + 1)/2▮)
